index 7a3126a..40e0e73 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -67,14 +67,36 @@ ## User Administration
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to **one** entity and has a `name`, a `slug` unique within the entity and an `is_active` flag (default on). Issuing a ticket into an inactive queue is rejected.
+
 ### Ticket
 
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
+- Display code (see below).
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default) or `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` or `called`. There is no cancelled status.
+
+**Display code:** per queue, the letter `A` followed by at least three digits, zero padded: `A001`, `A002`, … `A999`, then `A1000`, `A1001`, … The next code is the **last well-formed code by insertion order plus one** (so `A999` followed by `A1000` yields `A1001`). Malformed codes that are not `A<digits>` are skipped. Deleting a ticket does not renumber the tickets issued after it. Codes are unique per queue.
+
+**Issuance:**
+
+- New tickets are `waiting`, with `issued_at` set to now, channel `virtual` and priority `0` unless given.
+- A negative priority is rejected.
+- The queue's `is_active` flag is checked from the database inside the issuing transaction, under a row lock. A queue deactivated after the caller loaded it still rejects issuance.
+- A rejected issuance persists nothing.
+
+**Single call:**
+
+- Calling a waiting ticket marks it `called` and records `called_at` and the calling user.
+- Only members of the ticket's entity, with any role, may call it. Anyone else is rejected and the ticket is unchanged.
+- A ticket that is not waiting cannot be called again.
+- Choosing *which* ticket is called next (ordering and fairness below) is not implemented yet.
 
 ### Priority
 
